+
+## Native parametric family — review-6577472d8bd4ca54
+
+The production generator and canonical rule remain unchanged. The task-local native family adds `finish_rule=classify_only` as the byte-exact canonical default and `finish_rule=classify_then_highlight_armiest` as a composed alternative. Stage A performs canonical arm/room classification; Stage B counts the red arm cells in each completed multicolor component and recolors the cyan cells of the unique maximum to color 4.
+
+The minimum two-example lesson deliberately reverses total-size ordering and includes a two-room bridge whose canonical red arm cells are not recoverable from raw degree-one tips. This repaired an intermediate sampler defect where “choose the smallest component” and “choose the object with most raw tips” could replace the intended intermediate. A finite protected-Racket audit covers both settings at seeds 0 and 17 against size, cyan-count, scan-order, raw-tip, identity, and opposite-setting rivals; none survives demonstrations and changes a query. This is bounded evidence, not universal identifiability.
+
+The family supports 2–6 demonstrations and 1–4 prefix-stable queries on setting-independent inputs. Query four is 30×30 and touches all four boundaries. Native qualification and deterministic replay passed on both settings and seeds 0/17. The retained wrong-intermediate witness substitutes total component size for classified red-arm count and changes 13 output cells. Owner integration, fresh acceptance replay, and any training-admission decision remain pending.
